4. In each frame, the function calculates the new angle and velocity using simple harmonic motion (gravity is simulated by a negative force proportional to the sine of the angle).
5. If the pendulum has stopped oscillating (i.e., the velocity is very small), the function stops updating the angle and velocity.
6. The `drawPendulum()` function is called to redraw the pendulum on the canvas, using the current angle and position.

